Hi RGRN!

Recently i read about lethe patch in slashem & nethack differences
list. I thought "Cool!" and downloaded the patch to examine it a bit. I
quickly discovered that it wasn't fully integrated into slashem. After
asking a few people I heard that someone started integrating it, but
ran out of interest. As I'm sort of person that doesn't like to wait, I
considered integrating it myself. So here is result of my play with S
code: http://markosc.w.interia.pl/Slethe-1.1.patch - lethe patch remade
for slashem 0.0.7E7.

It adds:
 - scrolls of demonology and elementalism - yet another reason not to
read-id scrolls
 - silver capped staff (yet another silver weapon)
 - Python sketch: dead parrots are revived by shopkeepers
     ("You're not dead! You're only resting!")
 - failed arfifact wishes now include cool message from Moloch as well
as summoning a few his minions
 - new dungeon branch between Dungeons of Doom and Gehennom: Lethe
Gorge - 9 new levels, castle being the third level of it
 - under-castle branch with one level
 - Gates of Gehennom as last level of Lethe Gorge, with Cerberus as a
guard
 - Demon lairs, Valley of the Dead and Sanctum levels changed to Lethe
versions
 - Pleasent Valley - nice level in Gehennom with branch to Vlad's Tower
 - Cthulhu (another demon prince, worse even than Demogorgon) is new
Moloch's high priest
 - Wizard's Tower is another dungeon branch (just like Vlad's Tower)
 - Gulf of N'kai (4 special levels) at bottom of Gehennom (second one
of them has portal to Wizard's Tower, the last one is Vibrating Square
level)

Note that dungeon is now REALLY big and crowded (over 70 levels deep!).

Hope you will enjoy this patch!


